text:
megan: Kickoff for AxiomLabs reserved pool bring-up. Commitment: 14k RPS equiv. Need autoscale owner, loadtest window, and a cost-estimate for peak. Thoughts?

rahul: I’ll own the autoscale YAML. Quick Q: target latency p95? preferred GPUs to present to the customer?

megan: Targets: p95 <= 170ms for single-turn gen, <= 240ms for multi-turn chat. Customer prefers a100s but wants p4d tail numbers too. Traffic split: short 35% (<48), mid 50% (48-300), long 15% (>300).

zoe: I can run validation. Plan: shadow run first, then a 90m validation: smoke 20m, ramp 20m, soak 50m. Need ephemeral creds + traffic CSV. Suggest window Fri 01:00-03:00 UTC (low impact).

tyler: Ops guidance: mixed triggers - queue_len>160 OR gpu_mem_pct>80% OR p95>160ms sustained 20s => scale-up. Scale-down when all under thresholds for 3m. Cooldowns: up=20s, down=120s. min_replicas=4, max_replicas=32. Add fallback route to `redwood-slim` if available_capacity < 12%. Alert if fallback_rate > 1%.

rahul: Sounds good. Will include mem+queue triggers and a soft cap on concurrent streams per GPU (28) to avoid OOMs. Batching targets: short=5 tokens/batch, mid=7, long=3. Will post YAML draft shortly.

zoe: k6 harness I'll use (attaches traffic CSV separately):
```js
import http from 'k6/http';
import { sleep } from 'k6';
const lines = open('axiom_traffic.csv').split('
');
export default function(){
  const body = {input: lines[Math.floor(Math.random()*lines.length)]};
  http.post('https://api.redwood.example/v1/generate', JSON.stringify(body), { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${__ENV.TOKEN}` } });
  sleep(0.02);
}
```

megan: @ops-bot please create ephemeral token for zoe and schedule the run if we confirm the window. Also include a note to prime KV for top-30 prompts before the smoke.

ops-bot: Ephemeral token created: tok-ax-1122 (expires in 4 hours). Runbook doc created: rb-ax-1122 (private). Tentative scheduled window: 2025-04-11 01:00-03:00 UTC. Audit id: aud-7123.

tyler: Runbook checklist to include: pre-warm KV (top-30), model cache prime, smoke at 10% for 20m, ramp 20m linear to peak, soak 50m at peak, failure injection (kill one worker at 30m to validate fallback), post-checks (latency histograms, tokens_per_batch distribution, fallback_ratio, OOMs, errors.rate). Capture per-token cost estimate for peak.

rahul: I'll open the PR with autoscale YAML + tunables + checklist by EOD. Zoe, please attach the traffic CSV and the exact k6 commands in the runbook.

zoe: Will do. I'll run a quick shadow today to sanity-check the script and post initial perf graphs + rough peak egress/cost estimate in the runbooks channel.

megan: I'll notify the AxiomLabs account lead and ask them to be available for the first 15m of soak for a subjective quality check. Thanks everyone.
